 "tray_min_pt": 88,
 "_tray_note": "A real tangram's small triangles are genuinely small (each is 1/16 of the square), so pieces fall under the 88 pt minimum on a small stage. Do NOT fatten them: that stops it being a tangram. Render each piece on the TRAY at max(trueSize, 88 pt) and shrink it to true size as it approaches its slot. Take stays >= 88 pt, Hold stays true size.",
 "_tray_scale_warning": "'tray_scale_authored' is the enlargement needed AT THIS FRAME SIZE (fit 1.0) and is authored intent plus a sanity check — NOT a final number. The scene is fitted to the stage, so the factor differs per device; a baked constant scales down with everything else and preserves the shortfall. The engine must compute the tray scale at layout time from the size the piece was actually laid out at, and must never render a Take surface under 88 pt.",
 "_focus_note": "The scene is mostly sky and ground; the puzzle is the cat. Fit 'focus' to the stage rather than the whole frame and the pieces grow by about half on a phone — the small triangle goes from 31 pt to 46 pt at 844x390. The scene art still draws full-bleed behind it; only the puzzle's working area is fitted.",
